    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d265-a4">

                <pb facs="0365" n="291" sameAs="frus:frus1866p2/pg291"/>


                <head>Mr. Webb to Admiral Godon.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United United,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Petropolis,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-09-16"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 16, 1866</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reply to your official note of
                    yesterday, received at 7 p.m. this evening, I have the pleasure to communicate
                    for your information that on the 22d of August I advised Mr. <pb facs="0366"
                        n="292" xml:id="pg292"/> Washburn officially that all obstructions on the
                    part of the allied fleet to his repairing to his post of duty had been
                    removed.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. WATSON WEBB.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Acting Rear-Admiral <hi rendition="#small-caps">S. W. Godon,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Commanding United States South Atlantic
                            Squadron.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
